            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Why can't we just switch to Item.System now? \nIs there a separate commit to do that?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "> Why can't we just switch to Item.System now?\n\nWe could, if we move the HostIndex property from ManagedHost interface to Item.System. However, depending on how we want to proceed with merging single- and multi-host paths, we might not need the property.  \n\nI'll try to follow-up with a discord thread today, where we should discuss the merge strategy for single- and multi-host code paths to get all on the same page.\n\nResolving this for now."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 212,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@gmx.de",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "I wonder if we can use Item.System here as well. \n\n\nIs there any good reason to not move the property ist 'HostIndex' over to Item.System?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 212,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "That depends on whether we need that property long term. Currently that might not be the case, if we decide to go with associations for everything. \n\nIf that would not be the case I agree, we should think about implementing it on Item.System."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 212,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@gmx.de",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you explain how associations may help in avoiding the property?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 212,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Same as with inventory related associations. For those, we don't need the property too."
                }
            ],
